sev.better_fix:
Do not add a reversible "depositsPaused" flag that gates topUp. It gives the admin a new power, selectively blocking owners or helpers from funding vaults. That contradicts the published "We turn evil: we can only pause new vault creation" promise, and every public page would then need rewording.

If v2 wants an on-chain brake, make it a one-way deprecate()/sunset() that:
- permanently blocks createVault and topUp and cannot be undone;
- never touches checkIn, withdraw, setBeneficiary, initiateClaim, abortClaim, finalizeClaim or withdrawCredit;
- emits a Deprecated event;
- is disclosed as an admin power on README, index, how-it-works and security.html.

Because it is irreversible, it cannot be used to grief one vault at a time.

For the deployed immutable contract, the remedy is off-chain:
- the front-end disables topUp once a migration is announced;
- the migration notice tells owners to withdraw in full, which moves the vault to STATE_CLOSED and makes topUp revert, rather than leaving dust in it;
- SECURITY.md states that deposits into existing vaults cannot be halted on-chain.
